musig2 — provenance note
=========================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `bip340`
module, and `tlsresume`/`dtls`/`falcon`/`slhdsa` — self-contained crypto
modules not folded into the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

musig2 — clean-room implementation from BIP327 ("MuSig2 for
BIP340-compatible Multi-Signatures", bitcoin/bips), covering: key
aggregation and the "second key"/coefficient rule ("Key Generation and
Aggregation"), key tweaking ("Applying Tweaks"/"Tweaking Definition" —
plain and x-only, with the gacc/tacc accumulators), nonce generation and
aggregation ("Nonce Generation", "Nonce Aggregation"), the
session-context/challenge construction ("Session Context"), signing,
partial-signature verification, and partial-signature aggregation
("Signing", "Partial Signature Verification", "Partial Signature
Aggregation"). BIP327 is a public, open Bitcoin Improvement
Proposal — not a copyrightable work (merger doctrine; see
CONVENTIONS.md §5) — so no third-party-source NOTICE entry is strictly
required for the spec citation alone. No reference implementation's
source was ported or consulted as a design reference — this scaffolding
pass worked from the BIP327 specification text
(`bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0327.mediawiki`) and the public API of
`std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1` plus the sibling `bip340` module only (no
`bitcoin-core/secp256k1`, no `jonasnick/bip327`/`sipa`-authored reference
Python, or other implementation consulted for algorithm shape or code).

The official BIP327 test vectors (`kat_vectors.zig`) were fetched directly
from the JSON files under `bip-0327/vectors/` in the `bitcoin/bips`
repository:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/key_agg_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/key_sort_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/nonce_gen_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/nonce_agg_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/sign_verify_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/sig_agg_vectors.json
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitcoin/bips/master/bip-0327/vectors/tweak_vectors.json
These are public specification artifacts — the BIP's own published
conformance vectors — not copied from any other implementation's test
suite. `tweak_vectors.json` (and key_agg_vectors.json's two tweak error
cases) were embedded in the tweaking pass. One published vector file was
fetched but NOT embedded: `det_sign_vectors.json` (the optional
single-signer `DeterministicSign` convenience wrapper, not part of the
core signing flow implemented here).

`std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1` / `std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256` (MIT, part of
Zig itself) and the sibling `bip340` module (this repository, MIT — see
`../bip340/NOTICE`) are used via their public APIs; no new curve or hash
primitive is implemented here.

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.

**Status: complete (v2, tweak-aware).** The full BIP327 core signing flow
(wire codecs, `KeySort`, `NonceGen`, `KeyAgg`, `NonceAgg`,
`GetSessionValues`, `Sign` with the mandatory self-verify,
`PartialSigVerify`, `PartialSigAgg`) and key tweaking (`ApplyTweak`,
plain + x-only, composing via the gacc/tacc accumulators) are implemented
and byte-exact against the official BIP327 vectors; the aggregate
signature verifies under plain `bip340.verify` against the (possibly
tweaked) aggregate key. Every implementation pass — scaffold, crypto
core, and tweaking — worked from the BIP327 specification text only (no
reference implementation consulted). `DeterministicSign` remains out of
scope — see `SPEC.md`'s "Out of scope" and "Done record".
